UJI KAZUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>USAMI MITSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUNOBU CHIZUKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAMESHIMA, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKARAGI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJI, KAZUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>USAMI, MITSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUNOBU, CHIZUKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for effectively preventing a forgery of paper or film-form medium, wherein, for one solution, a thin, antenna-equipped semiconductor chip up to 0.5 mm square is embedded in a medium with the side walls of the chip formed with oxide films and separated from the chip by etching. Limiting the size of the semiconductor chip to up to 0.5 mm can improve resistances against bending and concentrated over loading, etching separation can provide a crack-, breakage-free semiconductor chip, and oxide films on the side walls require a simple process in preventing short-circuiting at edges when bonded to an antenna.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé qui permet d'empêcher effectivement la contrefaçon d'un support en papier ou en film. Dans une forme de réalisation, une microplaquette semiconductrice mince d'au plus 0,5 mm carré équipée d'une antenne est intégrée à un support. Les parois latérales de la microplaquette sont formées de couches d'oxyde et séparées de la microplaquette par gravure. La limitation de la taille de la microplaquette à des dimensions d'au plus 0,5 mm permet d'améliorer sa résistance à la flexion et à la surcharge concentrée. La séparation par gravure donne une microplaquette semiconductrice exempte de fissures ou de fragmentations. Le dépôt des couches d'oxyde sur les parois latérales s'effectue au moyen d'un simple procédé qui empêche les court-circuitages sur des bords, lorsque la microplaquette est équipée d'une antenne.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>